  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>89</mn></msub><mi>Ac</mi><msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>103</mn></msub><mi>Lr</mi></math></p><p>Belongs to actinoids series and they all belongs to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>rd</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;group. So atomic n o.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>101</mn></math>&nbsp;element is actinoids and atomic number&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>104</mn></math>&nbsp;element belongs to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>th</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;group.&nbsp;</p>",
